<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Close of play scores on the opening</p>
<p>day of four-day English county championship cricket matches on</p>
<p>Wednesday:</p>
<p>Canterbury: Kent 203-4 (A.Wells 102 not out, G.Cowdrey 53) v</p>
<p>Essex.</p>
<p>Blackpool: Warwickshire 139 (P.Martin 6-46; I.Austin 4-45).</p>
<p>Lancashire 192-3 (G.Lloyd 70 not out, N H Fairbrother 58).</p>
<p>Lord's:  Middlesex 212-3 (M.Ramprakash 99 not out) v</p>
<p>Hampshire.</p>
<p>Northampton: Worcestershire 433-5 (W.Weston 196 not out, D.</p>
<p>Leatherdale 110) v Northamptonshire.</p>
<p>The Oval: Surrey 164-2 (J.Ratcliffe 54 not out) v Durham.</p>
</text>
